The Keycloak Service is the central Identity and Access Management (IAM) and Identity Provider (IdP) of the system, managing authentication (AuthN) and authorization (AuthZ) for all applications. It offers a unified login page and uses the OpenID Connect (OIDC) protocol for secure token-based access. Keycloak integrates with the Mock Backoffice Application to authenticate users, issue tokens, and enforce consistent access policies through defined realms, roles, and groups.